{title: Beulah Land}
{artist: Edgar P. Stites / John R. Sweney}
{genre: Gospel}
{style: Traditional}
{flow: Closing, Meditative}
{key: G}
{tempo: 72}
{time: 4/4}

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
I've [G]reached the land of [C]corn and [G]wine
And [D7]all its riches [G]freely mine
Here [G]shines undimmed one [C]blissful [G]day
For [D7]all my night has passed a[G]way
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus}
O [G]Beulah Land, sweet [C]Beulah [G]Land
As [D7]on thy highest mount I [G]stand
I [G]look away a[C]cross the [G]sea
Where [D7]mansions are pre[G]pared for me
And [G]view the shining [C]glory [G]shore
My [D7]heaven, my [G]home for[D7]ever[G]more
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
My [G]Saviour comes and [C]walks with [G]me
And [D7]sweet communion [G]here have we
He [G]gently leads me [C]by His [G]hand
For [D7]this is heaven's border [G]land
{end_of_verse}

{chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
A [G]sweet perfume up[C]on the [G]breeze
Is [D7]borne from ever [G]vernal trees
And [G]flowers that never [C]fade nor [G]die
Bloom [D7]in the fields of para[G]dise
{end_of_verse}

{chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 4}
The [G]zephyrs seem to [C]float to [G]me
Sweet [D7]sounds of heaven's [G]melody
As [G]angel-wings, with [C]ceaseless [G]sweep
Move [D7]o'er the Jasper [G]Sea
{end_of_verse}

{chorus}
